			<xs:element name="Securitisation" minOccurs="0">
				<xs:annotation>
					<xs:appinfo source="@since 4.2.12"/>
					<xs:documentation xml:lang="en">56_Securitisation
alpha (1)
"a" refers to the fact that the asset managers have not assessed the eligibility of a treatment of the securitisation positions under Solvency II
"b" refers to security positions eligible for art 178 (3) and art 178 (5) (Senior STS)
"c" refers to security positions eligible for art 178 (4) and art 178 (6) (Junior STS)
"d" refers to resecuritisation positions as per art 178(7) (re-securitisation)
"e1" refers to securitisation positions as per Art 178 (8). (senior non STS)
"e2" refers to securitisation positions as per Art 178 (8a). (junior non STS)
"e3" refers to securitisation positions as per Art 178 (9 ). (others)
"f" refers to security positions eligible for art 178a (1) &amp; (2) (transitional regime for type 1 securitisations without new underlying exposure since the 01/01/2019)
"g" refers to security positions eligible for art 178a (3) (transitional regime for some type 1 securitisations on residential mortgages)
"h"refers to security positions eligible for art 178a (4). (transitional regime for some type 1 securitisations on residential mortgages)
"i" refers to security positions eligible for art 180 (10) and art 180 (10a). (Securitisation secured by the EIB or the EIF)
"j" refers to security positions that have been analysed and shall not be considered as "securitisation " under Solvency 2 (No securitisation).</xs:documentation>
				</xs:annotation>
